## How to Use

1. When an error occurs during any stage, append an entry here.
2. Link to the corresponding fix in `fix.log` using the entry date + stage as a key.
3. After resolving, update `lessons_learned.md` with what was learned.

## Common Error Patterns

| Pattern | Stage | Resolution Link |
|---------|-------|-----------------|
| GitHub Actions build failure | CI/CD | See fix.log |
| Navigation config mismatch | UI | See fix.log |
| Markdown render 404 | 6_Semblance | See fix.log |
| Azure Key Vault access denied | Secrets | See fix.log |
[2026-07-12] [7_Testing_Known] [ERROR] — Smoke test failure: Menu Links Resolve (cloud mode). 8 stage folder header links 404 on GitHub Pages (bare directory URLs, no index.html in stage folders). GitHub Issue: https://github.com/rifaterdemsahin/delivery-pilot-template/issues/1
[2026-09-10] [2_Environment] [ERROR] — kagent install on minikube: every pod (`kagent-controller`, `kagent-ui`, `kagent-tools`, etc.) stuck `ImagePullBackOff`. Root cause: a pre-existing Zarf mutating admission webhook (from an unrelated prior `zarf`/`hello-world` PoC on the same cluster) rewrites image references cluster-wide (every namespace except `kube-system`) to route through its own local pull-through registry, which had never mirrored kagent's images.
[2026-09-10] [2_Environment] [WARNING] — kagent CLI `KAGENT_HELM_EXTRA_ARGS` env var does a naive `strings.Split(s, "--set")`; surrounding whitespace in the value leaked into the generated Helm `--set` flags, producing a stray top-level key `' providers'` (leading space) and a model name with a trailing space (`'deepseek-chat '`) instead of the intended `providers.openAI.config.baseUrl` override.
[2026-09-10] [4_Formula] [INFO] — `helm get values kagent -n kagent` printed the DeepSeek API key in plaintext to terminal output while diagnosing the above. Not committed anywhere; treated as sensitive from that point on (rebuilt the fix from the source env var, not from the dumped output).
[2026-09-10] [7_Testing_Known] [ERROR] — Live agent invoke against `k8s-agent` reached DeepSeek successfully (config confirmed correct) but DeepSeek's API returned `402 Payment Required — Insufficient Balance`, blocking KR 2.2 (run sample agents in Kubernetes — produce a real response). Logged as risk R-010 in `1_Real_Unknown/risks.md`.
[2026-09-10] [5_Symbols] [ERROR] — kagent-flyio Docker build: `apk add` failed on `rancher/k3s:v1.31.4-k3s1` — that image is minimal BusyBox with no package manager at all.
[2026-09-10] [5_Symbols] [ERROR] — kagent-flyio Docker build: `wget https://get.helm.sh/...` inside the k3s image failed with `wget: not an http or ftp url` — BusyBox's `wget` in this image was compiled without TLS support and cannot fetch any `https://` URL.
[2026-09-10] [7_Testing_Known] [ERROR] — First live invoke against the Fly.io deployment (`kagent-k3s.fly.dev`) failed: `OpenAI chat completion request failed: ... dial tcp: lookup api.deepseek.com on 10.43.0.10:53: server misbehaving`. Root cause: Fly Machines default `/etc/resolv.conf` to Fly's internal-only 6PN resolver (`fdaa::3`), which only resolves `*.internal` names; k3s's CoreDNS forwards upstream queries to that file by default, so all public DNS lookups failed.
